List @[`modelFallbackMiddleware`] before `modelRefusalMiddleware`, as in the example above. When the model refuses, the fallback middleware retries the request on the next model, which can be from the same provider or a different one. A fallback model can still refuse the same request. Combine this with one of the other options for when every model refuses.





To reply to the user instead of failing the run when every model refuses, add a middleware before `modelFallbackMiddleware` that catches the error:

```typescript

AIMessage,
createAgent,
createMiddleware,
modelFallbackMiddleware,
modelRefusalMiddleware,
} from "langchain";

```typescript

